## Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

### Summary
Verified and completed the installation of Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Status: ✅ Already Configured

The project already had Vercel Web Analytics properly configured:
- The `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was listed in package.json dependencies
- The Analytics component was already imported and implemented in the root layout

### Changes Made

**Modified:**
- `package-lock.json` - Updated to include @vercel/analytics@2.0.1 package metadata after running `npm install`

**No code changes were required** - The implementation was already complete and correct according to the official Vercel documentation.

### Implementation Details

**Framework:** Next.js 16.3.8 (App Router)

**Configuration Location:** `app/layout.tsx`
- Imported: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Component added at the end of `<body>` tag: `<Analytics />`

This follows the exact pattern recommended in the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Next.js App Router projects.

### Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. ✅ Verified project uses Next.js App Router framework
3. ✅ Confirmed @vercel/analytics@2.0.1 is in package.json
4. ✅ Ran `npm install` to ensure dependencies are properly installed
5. ✅ Verified Analytics component correctly imported from "@vercel/analytics/next"
6. ✅ Confirmed `<Analytics />` component placed in root layout.tsx
7. ✅ TypeScript type checking passed with `npm run typecheck`
8. ✅ Production build completed successfully with `npm run build`
9. ✅ All 59 tests passed with `npm test`

### Next Steps for Full Activation

To start collecting analytics data, you'll need to:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics → Enable)
2. Deploy this project to Vercel
3. After deployment, analytics will automatically start tracking page views and web vitals

The code implementation is complete and production-ready.
